WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.957
A quick trick for case maths: the rule of seventy two.

2
00:00:04.057 --> 00:00:07.871
A market grows 8% a year. How long to double?

3
00:00:08.021 --> 00:00:10.461
Years to double ≈ 72 ÷ growth rate

4
00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:12.753
72 ÷ 8

5
00:00:12.853 --> 00:00:14.155
≈ 9 years

6
00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:19.742
It works the other way too: to double in six years, you need about twelve percent a year.
